<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hasanwayhids</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 959–1015</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Hasanuyids</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hasanwayhids were a Kurdish dynasty that ruled parts of the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagros-mountains">Zagros</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dinavar">Dinawar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kermanshah">Kermanshah</a>, from about 959 to 1015. Founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hasanwayh-ibn-husayn">Hasanwayh ibn Husayn</a>, chief of the Barzikani <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurds">Kurds</a>, it reached its height under his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badr-ibn-hasanwayh">Badr ibn Hasanwayh</a>, who was recognised by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buyid-dynasty">Buyids</a> and the Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a>. After Badr's death the dynasty declined and lost its lands to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kakuyids">Kakuyids</a> and others.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hasanwayhids.jpg" alt="Hasanwayhids" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Selfbell · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hasanwayhids-map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
